# Secrets — each machine keeps its own; .env.example is the committed template.
.env

# Virtualenvs are architecture- and path-specific. Never put one in this folder
# if the folder lives on a NAS: paddle_venv already proved that, its pyvenv.cfg
# still points at a Homebrew path and a scratchpad directory that is long gone.
env/
venv/
.venv/
paddle_venv/

# 10Hz frame captures. 1.3G and growing; history, not input.
screenshot_log/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# --- added 2026-09-05, when this finally became a git repo ------------------
#
# What is versioned: code, config, docs, and the SMALL data the code cannot run
# without (world_map.json, places/, route*_steps.json). What is not: build
# trees, recorded media, and anything a run regenerates.
#
# The rule for anything borderline: if losing it would only cost time, ignore
# it. If losing it would cost a MEASUREMENT that cannot be retaken, commit it.

# Its own git checkout, and the artefacts built from it. The patch that matters
# lives in chiaki-patch/ and is versioned there.
chiaki-ng-src/
chiaki-ng-build/

# Recorded media. Large, regenerable, and history rather than input.
# NOTE: demos/walk3_full_20260828_050731 and demos/walk_20260827_214446 ARE
# referenced by build_world_map.py, go.py, anchors.py and two tests — they are
# ignored here because of size, not because they are disposable. Do not delete
# them from disk.
demos/
world_log/
explore/
diagnostics/
route_frames/
hand_samples/
Photos to train on/
Photos of ban screen missing cards/

# test_fixtures/ IS VERSIONED, deliberately, despite being ~180M of images.
#
# A test whose data is not committed is a test that cannot be run from a fresh
# clone, and this suite's entire value is that it runs offline anywhere. 30
# tests read these. Excluding them for size would mean the repo contains tests
# that provably do not work — which is worse than a large repo.
#
# Images do not delta-compress, so a fixture that CHANGES costs its full size
# again in history. Fixtures here are captured once and read forever, so that
# is a bounded cost. Recaptured frames should replace a directory wholesale
# rather than being appended alongside the old ones.

# Run outputs and hand-made backups, now that history is real.
overnight/*.log
overnight/*.json
overnight/*failframes*/        # frames a run writes; regenerated each time
overnight/phase1/
overnight/failframes/

# Machine-local calibration and run state. compass_scale.json and
# view_bounds.json are keyed on a machine id and rebuilt on first use;
# progress_testing.json is live run state, not source.
compass_scale.json
view_bounds.json
progress_testing.json
progress.json
leg_reliability.json
*.backup_*
world_map.json.backup_*
CLAUDE.md.backup_*
places_backup_*/
tests_quarantine/__pycache__/

# Screenshot archives (spaces in the names; no quotes — git takes those
# literally and the pattern silently matches nothing).
/Photos*/          # only at the project ROOT, not test_fixtures/gameplay_photos

# Subagent scratch notes — see agent_progress/README.md
agent_progress/*
!agent_progress/README.md
.console_busy
